From ecac2a072ac34b23d87c909d95aca9d87b409775 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:49:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 137/138] dynarmic A64: SBFM/UBFM as shifts; W values zero
 above 32 bits stored and widened as they are

bitfield_shifts: SBFM and UBFM by immediate (LSL, LSR, UBFX, UBFIZ, SBFX, SBFIZ, UXTB, UXTH) as one
shift, a shift and an AND with an imm32 mask, or a left shift then a right one, instead of the
architecture's rotate and two masks (rorx, movabs, and, and; nine instructions for SBFIZ #n, #32).
With skip_redundant_extensions: a W register's value that is zero above 32 bits in its host
register by how it was made (EmitX64::GprZeroUpper32: 32-bit x64 operations, cmov, mov r32,
movzx, loads of 32 bits or fewer not sign-extended) is stored as it is, not copied and
zero-extended first (A64SetW), and widened to 64 bits as it is (ZeroExtendWordToLong); a
LeastSignificantWord whose every use reads the low 32 bits alone is the 64-bit value's register
(no mov r32, r32). game.c -4.7% instructions, unity.c -3.6%.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
